{"id":"u-c541d5db-2be5-4aaf-98d5-35068234a3de","src":"community","title":"5/3/1 BBS FSL (for athletes with back issues)","author":"Mishanya","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/mwRXNl-boring-but-smart-for-athletes-with-spinal-issues","desc":"This is my custom program for handling severe back pain and gaining muscle while still doing the main barbell movements. I have a l5-s1 hernia, a spondy and a facet syndrome so planned the exercises accordingly. Feel free to modify as appropriate.  \n\nTraining max should be 90% of the actual rep. max. After finishing the cycle, add no more than 2,5 kilos to pressing and 5 kilos to other main compounds. \n\nEach workout begins with a McGill Big Three drill to be repeated on rest days. All exercises before the main lift of the day are warmup drills. \n\nThe workouts require a trap bar, a belt squat and reverse hypers machines. \n\nRecommended to run for around a year before returning to competition lifts. \n\nConsider consulting a professional before starting. I share what works for me, may not work for you.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":80,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-16T11:17:32.803Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Seated Military Press","Trap Bar Deadlift","Bench Press","Front Squats"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Curl-Up","sets":[{"sec":60,"rpe":6}]},{"n":"Side Plank","sets":[{"sec":60,"rpe":6}]},{"n":"Bird Dog","sets":[{"sec":60,"rpe":6}]},{"n":"Reverse Hyperextension","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Cuban Press","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":6}]},{"n":"Seated Military Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":65},{"r":5,"pct":75},{"r":5,"pct":85}],"note":"Last set is a +set"},{"n":"Seated Military Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":65,"x":2}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n